        </param>
        <param>
          <type>uint32_t &amp;</type>
          <declname>payloadSize</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Decode the second to remaining byte(s) of a CCSDS Encap header, called after the DecodeCcsdsEncapHeaderSizeFromFirstByte function.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>encapHeaderLength</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The 1, 2, 4, or 8 byte size of encap packet expected to be decoded. This function need not be called if this value is 1. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>secondByte</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The pointer to the start of the second byte of the Encap header to decode. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>userDefinedField</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The returned user defined field of the Encap packet (usually 0) if encapHeaderLength is 4 or 8 bytes. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>payloadSize</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The returned payload size (i.e. size of the data being encapsulated) if encapHeaderLength is 2, 4, or 8 bytes. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>true on success (denoting valid userDefinedField and payloadSize), or false on failure. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
